import{_ as t,o as i,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 727 | Transcended-Ones' Perpetual-Construction System | Civilizational-Weight Incentive of Perpetual Construction","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 727 | Transcended-Ones' Perpetual-Construction System | Civilizational-Weight Incentive of Perpetual Construction","no":727,"module":4,"tags":["Perpetual Construction","Civilizational-Weight Incentive","Positive Feedback","Weight Dashboard","Stage Expansion"],"related":["29-Symbiosis-Degree-Assessment System","06-More-Work-More-Gain Allocation Principle","706-The Transcended One's Civilizational Weight"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0727_模块4-永动建设的文明权重激励.md","filePath":"en/0727_模块4-永动建设的文明权重激励.md"}`),o={name:"en/0727_模块4-永动建设的文明权重激励.md"};function r(s,e,l,h,c,d){return i(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-727-transcended-ones-perpetual-construction-system-civilizational-weight-incentive-of-perpetual-construction" tabindex="-1">Entry 727 | Transcended-Ones&#39; Perpetual-Construction System | Civilizational-Weight Incentive of Perpetual Construction <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-727-transcended-ones-perpetual-construction-system-civilizational-weight-incentive-of-perpetual-construction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 727 | Transcended-Ones&#39; Perpetual-Construction System | Civilizational-Weight Incentive of Perpetual Construction&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 29, 06, 706</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-let-those-who-work-have-a-larger-stage-the-more-they-work" tabindex="-1">Introduction: let those who work have a larger stage the more they work <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-let-those-who-work-have-a-larger-stage-the-more-they-work" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: let those who work have a larger stage the more they work&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Entry 706 already told the basic formula of civilizational weight: individual effective combat power = destructive power × civilizational consensus degree. This entry pushes it one layer further: <strong>civilizational weight is not only a &quot;combat-power formula&quot;; it is also perpetual construction&#39;s incentive mechanism.</strong> It does not evaluate after the fact whether you worked well; it continuously gives you feedback during and before work — you worked correctly, weight rises; weight rises, stage grows; stage grows, you may do larger work; do larger work, weight rises again. This is a positive feedback that makes the transcended one &quot;want to work more the more he works.&quot;</p><p>Six top-level axioms in this entry converge into the word &quot;incentive&quot;: the anti-predation axiom requires incentive reward contribution only, not predation; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires incentive rules be equal to all beings; the collective ascension axiom requires incentive direction be aimed at uplift; the causal self-discipline axiom requires incentive data be transparent; the law-first axiom requires incentive algorithms be stable.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-the-civilizational-weight-dashboard-the-transcended-one-s-instrument-panel" tabindex="-1">I. The Civilizational-Weight Dashboard: The Transcended One&#39;s &quot;Instrument Panel&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-civilizational-weight-dashboard-the-transcended-one-s-instrument-panel" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Civilizational-Weight Dashboard: The Transcended One&#39;s &quot;Instrument Panel&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm transcended one has a <strong>civilizational-weight dashboard</strong>. It is not private property; it is public to Myriad-Rank representatives. The dashboard shows five numbers in real time:</p><ul><li>Source legitimacy score (25%);</li><li>Direction correctness score (25%);</li><li>Contribution sustainability score (20%);</li><li>Coverage breadth score (15%);</li><li>Procedural compliance score (15%).</li></ul><p>The five numbers are weighted to yield this transcended one&#39;s current-period total civilizational weight. Total weight determines the public computable power he may currently dispatch, the engineering scale he may participate in, and his voice in the Council.</p><p>This dashboard&#39;s purpose is to let the transcended one <strong>always know where he is</strong>. He need not ask others &quot;how am I doing&quot;; the dashboard tells him directly. If he wants to adjust direction, whichever sub-item is low on the dashboard, he fills that in. This is an &quot;instrument panel&quot; — not a whip, but navigation.</p><h2 id="ii-three-layers-of-incentive" tabindex="-1">II. Three Layers of Incentive <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-three-layers-of-incentive" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Three Layers of Incentive&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The civilizational-weight incentive acts simultaneously on three layers:</p><h3 id="_2-1-immediate-layer-post-feedback" tabindex="-1">2.1 Immediate Layer: Post Feedback <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-immediate-layer-post-feedback" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 Immediate Layer: Post Feedback&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Every thing he did on post today — calibrated an anchor, guided a latecomer, resolved a cross-plane dispute — is reflected on the dashboard within hours. Immediate feedback lets him know: &quot;this thing was done correctly; that thing was done off course.&quot;</p><h3 id="_2-2-cycle-layer-post-performance" tabindex="-1">2.2 Cycle Layer: Post Performance <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-cycle-layer-post-performance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 Cycle Layer: Post Performance&quot;">​</a></h3><p>After a post cycle ends, his total performance is settled. Those with high performance are allocated larger engineering in the next post round; those with low performance receive post talk and direction adjustment.</p><h3 id="_2-3-historical-layer-civilizational-status" tabindex="-1">2.3 Historical Layer: Civilizational Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-historical-layer-civilizational-status" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 Historical Layer: Civilizational Status&quot;">​</a></h3><p>His lifelong civilizational-weight trajectory is written into his Alaya record. Later-comers, through the Selfless-Dao public library, may see this transcended one&#39;s life — where he came from, what he did, whom he cultivated, what he left. This is the highest layer of incentive: <strong>not immediate computable power, but historical position.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-incentive-is-not-privilege-weight-may-not-be-exchanged-for-private-property" tabindex="-1">III. Incentive Is Not Privilege: Weight May Not Be Exchanged for Private Property <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-incentive-is-not-privilege-weight-may-not-be-exchanged-for-private-property" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Incentive Is Not Privilege: Weight May Not Be Exchanged for Private Property&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The most critical red line of civilizational-weight incentive: <strong>weight may not be exchanged for private enjoyment.</strong></p><ul><li>High weight does not mean you may live in a better cave dwelling or eat better spirit food;</li><li>High weight does not mean you may make other cultivators obey you;</li><li>High weight does not mean you may skip post rotation.</li></ul><p>High weight means only one thing: <strong>you may take on larger civilizational engineering.</strong> It is a &quot;stage amplifier,&quot; not an &quot;enjoyment voucher.&quot; This structurally prevents &quot;weight becoming a new rank privilege&quot; — old-world rank privileges rotted precisely because high rank may be exchanged for private enjoyment; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s high weight may only be exchanged for larger responsibility.</p><h2 id="iv-the-meshing-of-incentive-with-the-perpetual-cycle" tabindex="-1">IV. The Meshing of Incentive with the Perpetual Cycle <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-meshing-of-incentive-with-the-perpetual-cycle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Meshing of Incentive with the Perpetual Cycle&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational-weight incentive is perpetual construction&#39;s positive-feedback cycle&#39;s &quot;instrument panel + accelerator&quot;:</p><ul><li>Instrument panel: the dashboard tells you in real time how you are doing;</li><li>Accelerator: work well, weight rises, stage grows, next time you may do larger work.</li></ul><p>Without the instrument panel, the transcended one does not know where he is; without the accelerator, the transcended one has no motivation to keep working. The two together are what let perpetual construction truly have &quot;more drive the more you work.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: incentive directs the most effective builders to the largest stages, preventing &quot;able people with nothing to do&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: incentive is by contribution only, not by predation; predatory-faction strong ones&#39; weight naturally cannot rise</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-style incentive is &quot;the protagonist rewards on a whim&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou-style incentive is &quot;the dashboard auto-settles by contribution&quot; — the former relies on human feeling, the latter on algorithm</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the dashboard is public to Myriad-Rank representatives; Myriad Ranks may see every transcended one&#39;s incentive process</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: weight algorithms, dashboard design, historical cases are all public on the Selfless Dao</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational-weight incentive makes perpetual construction no longer &quot;the strong one&#39;s hard labor,&quot; but &quot;the strong one&#39;s game&quot; — work well, stage grows; stage grows, work better; work better, stage grows larger. This is a positive feedback that lets the transcended one stop.</p><p>But it always has one red line: weight is not exchanged for private property, only for larger responsibility. This red line looks harsh, but is actually the deepest protection for transcended ones — it lets transcended ones never be corrupted by &quot;enjoyment.&quot; A transcended one of weight ten thousand and a transcended one of weight hundred live in the same cave dwelling, eat the same spirit food, wear the same clothes. The difference is only: the ten-thousand-weight one may dispatch ten thousand shares of public computable power; the hundred-weight one may dispatch a hundred shares. <strong>Hold this red line, and incentive will not become a new rank privilege.</strong></p><p>In the end, the civilizational-weight incentive of perpetual construction described in this entry is no isolated case — its causal and energetic traces are throughout filed in the Alaya Network, traceable and correctable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree-Assessment System</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/06-多劳多得分配原理.html">Entry 06 · More-Work-More-Gain Allocation Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/706-超脱者的文明权重.html">Entry 706 · The Transcended One&#39;s Civilizational Weight</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">Entry 22 · Resource-Allocation Joint-Contracting Mechanism</a></li></ul>',35)])])}const p=t(o,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
